# Canonicalize author identities for git log / shortlog / blame.
#
# This repo accumulated several author strings before anyone was paying attention:
# a name-vs-username difference, an email case difference, and — once work started
# on the shared DGX box — a hostname-derived address that git auto-invented from
# username@hostname because user.email was unset there.
#
# .mailmap fixes how git TOOLING reports these. It does not rewrite history, which
# is the point: the repo is cloned on two machines that sync only through GitHub,
# so rewriting published commits is not worth a cosmetic attribution fix.
#
# Note GitHub does not honour .mailmap for linking commits to accounts. Commits
# authored with vdp@neutrons-dgx01.ornl.gov will stay unlinked there; that address
# is not deliverable and so cannot be verified on the account. The fix for FUTURE
# commits is to set user.name and user.email on each machine — see CLAUDE.md.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> Commit Name <commit@email>

Daniel Pajerowski <daniel@pajerowski.com> dpaj <daniel@pajerowski.com>
Daniel Pajerowski <daniel@pajerowski.com> Daniel Pajerowski <Daniel@Pajerowski.com>
Daniel Pajerowski <daniel@pajerowski.com> Daniel Pajerowski (vdp) <vdp@neutrons-dgx01.ornl.gov>
